# Minecart route-stop relocation execution contract

Source proposal: `Docs/route-stop-relocation-proposal.md`

## Goal

Implement a fully wired route-stop relocation path for same-z minecart route markers so
`Relocate / Change location` opens a UserPrompt map-location flow, updates the native stop
position on confirmation, preserves route selection rendering behavior, and handles cancellation
safely.

## Assumptions and open questions

- `dwarfuicore/services` provides `UserPromptServiceProvider` with contract major `1`
  and `prompt_map_location` in the runtime used by this repository.
- A route-stop context menu callback can safely mutate `df.global.plotinfo.hauling` stop `pos`
  after defensive validation.
- `PROJECT` tracking is maintained through `Docs/project.todo` and is updated externally if needed.

## Phase 1: Add UserPrompt service dependency in DwarfUI

Outcome: DwarfUI can acquire a namespace-bound UserPrompt API without changing existing service
ownership contracts.

- [x] Extend `src/scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui/services.lua` to cache a `UserPromptService` API alongside
  `TooltipService` and `ContextMenuService`.
- [x] Add `UserPromptServiceProvider:new(CONTRACT_MAJOR, CONSUMER_NAMESPACE)` in `refresh()`.
- [x] Add `UserPromptService` module field with the same immutability pattern as other APIs.
- [x] Update `clear_namespaces()` to clear `UserPromptService` and propagate its result in the return value.
- [x] Keep provider construction non-destructive and compatible with existing reload/retirement flow.
- [x] Update service-shim smoke expectation points (if any local notes/tests reference only two DwarfUI services).
- [x] Verify the shim still initializes and clears namespaces cleanly under load and unload.

Completion criteria:

- [ ] `src/scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui/services.lua` exposes a namespace-bound
  `UserPromptService` and clears it in `clear_namespaces()`.
- [ ] No existing `TooltipService` / `ContextMenuService` behavior is changed.

## Phase 2: Replace placeholder relocation menu action with UserPrompt invocation

Outcome: Route-stop context-menu entries remain stable but now request map-location input instead of showing a
placeholder message.

- [x] Update `src/scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui-minecart-route-markers.lua`:
  - [x] Refactor `MinecartRouteMarkersOverlay:create_stop_context_menu_definition` to remove direct `dialogs.showMessage`
    for relocation.
  - [x] Add an `on_select` callback registration that calls
    `services.UserPromptService:prompt_map_location(...)`.
  - [x] Pass `title` and `message` strings that preserve user intent.
- [x] Capture immutable route/stop identity in the context-menu action handler scope so callback updates are
  route-scoped and not bound to stale pointer objects.
  - [x] Validate captured IDs are still present and matching before attempting to mutate any native data.
- [x] Add explicit `SERVICE_BUSY` handling:
  - [x] If `prompt_map_location` fails with active prompt contention, return no-op and preserve overlay state.
  - [x] Keep menu interaction behavior consistent for other stops while active prompt is denied.

Completion criteria:

- [ ] `Relocate / Change location` no longer calls placeholder alert text directly.
- [ ] Context-menu registration structure (`title` and entries) remains intact for route-stop items.
- [ ] A relocation attempt with an already busy prompt cannot mutate stop state and does not regress map registration.

## Phase 3: Implement safe relocation callback behavior

Outcome: Confirmed left-click selection updates stop location; cancellation and stale-state paths do not mutate invalid
targets.

- [x] In `on_select(position)` implement idempotent callback flow:
  - [x] Resolve current `df.global.plotinfo.hauling` fresh.
  - [x] Re-resolve route by id and stop by id under current state.
  - [x] Require route and stop identity match before writing.
  - [x] No-op on missing/invalid/`nil` input position.
  - [x] Write a detached copy of `{x, y, z}` to the matched stop position.
- [x] In `on_cancel`, return without any mutation and without side effects.
- [x] Preserve existing selection state where practical:
  - [x] Ensure relocation completion refreshes via existing selected-route overlay/render sync.
  - [x] Avoid introducing separate marker-selection mutation logic.

Completion criteria:

- [ ] A valid selection updates only the intended same-z stop position.
- [ ] A canceled selection leaves stop position untouched.
- [ ] Stale route/stop identity callbacks are ignored without throw.
- [ ] Existing overlay teardown and selection-clear semantics still pass through unchanged.

## Phase 4: Update verification and migration tasks

Outcome: Plan and tests explicitly cover unit, native, and project-tracking expectations without implementing behavior changes.

- [x] Update `tests/minecart_route_overlay.spec.lua` to mock `services.UserPromptService` and validate:
  - [x] `create_stop_context_menu_definition` wires relocation entry to prompt.
  - [x] `on_select` callback writes expected stop position.
  - [x] `on_cancel` does not mutate stop data.
  - [x] stale-id / missing-stop callback guards exist.
- [x] Update `tests/minecart_route/route_stop_context_menu.ds.lua` to validate end-to-end native relocation flow.
  - [x] Left-click path in prompt updates stop position and returns to Hauling menu.
  - [x] Right-click or `LEAVESCREEN` in prompt leaves stop unchanged and closes/returns cleanly.
  - [x] Existing "Zoom to this stop" and non-z marker behaviors remain represented.
- [x] Decide whether `Docs/project.todo` gets the route-stop status update in this plan or remains delegated to owner.

Completion criteria:

- [ ] Unit and native acceptance checks for relocation are added and mapped to explicit assertions.
- [ ] Route-stop placeholder path no longer has direct placeholder coverage dependency.
- [ ] `Docs/route-stop-relocation-proposal.md` requirements map to at least one `.todo` task each.

## Final acceptance

- [ ] Every proposal requirement is implemented or explicitly deferred with rationale.
- [ ] Existing context-menu + tooltip registrations remain stable and teardown-clean.
- [ ] Required source, unit, and native coverage changes are present and complete.
- [ ] No implementation work is performed inside this planning artifact.
